# oracle: pair_style srp with the minimum-distance option (srp 0.8 * min exclude yes: every bond type, the lever rule) over two runs of 20 steps (the bond particles are deleted after the first run and inserted again at the second run's setup), on examples/PACKAGES/srp/in.srp cut down (3000 DPD beads in chains, 2700 bonds, bond particles of type 2 inserted at the bond midpoints at the setup, excluded from type 1, in no group; newton on on, comm_modify cutoff 3.6). w206sr_chain.data is examples/PACKAGES/srp/data.chain byte for byte.
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native thermo max rel 1.6e-14, final per-atom state max rel 1.4e-11 (the DPD random numbers drawn in native pair order with the bond particles in native's sorted storage).
# oracle-inputs: w206sr_chain.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      full
boundary p p p
special_bonds lj/coul 1 1 1
newton on on
read_data w206sr_chain.data
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 10 check yes
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      * 225.0 0.85
comm_modify vel yes
comm_modify cutoff 3.6
pair_style      hybrid dpd 1.0 1.0 373692 srp 0.8 * min exclude yes
pair_coeff      1 1 dpd 60.0 4.5 1.0
pair_coeff      1 2 none
pair_coeff      2 2 srp 100.0
variable        natoms equal count(all)
variable        nPotEng equal c_thermo_pe/v_natoms
thermo 10
thermo_style custom step temp pe v_nPotEng press atoms v_natoms lx ly lz
thermo_modify format float %.15g
fix  1 all nve
timestep        0.01
run          20
run          20
